-- title:
--   Rank comparison for local Hecke algebras at level S₀ ⊆ S
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k =$ `ResidueField 𝒪`, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is a two-dimensional $k$-vector space `ρbar.V` with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to its endomorphisms which is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite subextension of $\mathbb{Q}$; assume $\bar\rho$ absolutely irreducible, i.e. the base change to $\overline{k} \otimes_k$ `ρbar.V` has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of natural numbers with every element of $S$ prime and $p \in S$, and let $N \neq 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$ and none in $S_0$, with $p^2 \nmid N$. Local conditions are imposed on $\bar\rho$: it is unramified at the $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$, $q \nmid N$ (every element of the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $q$ acts as the identity); for primes $q \neq p$ with $q \parallel N$ it is ramified at $q$ and inertia at $q$ acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for primes $q \neq p$ with $q^2 \mid N$ one has $q^3 \nmid N$ and again unipotent inertia at $q$; and if $p \mid N$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ in the sense of `GaloisRep_LocalConditions.IsOrdinaryAt`. Assume that weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are $\mathbb{C}$-spanned by those with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin T$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin T$. Let $\theta' :$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀` $\to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose values are prescribed by $\bar\rho$: for primes $\ell \neq p$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for a valuation subring over $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta'(T_\ell) X + \ell$; $\theta'(U_q) = 0$ for primes $q$ with $q^2 \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$; and for $q \parallel N$, $q \notin S_0$, respectively for $T_p$ when $p \nmid N$ and $p \notin S_0$, the value is the trace of any endomorphism of the quotient of `ρbar.V` by $\sum_{\tau \in I_q} \mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau) - 1)$ induced by a Frobenius element at $q$ (resp. at $p$). Finally let $\theta$ on `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` be the restriction of $\theta'$ along the inclusion coming from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L45). Then the rank over $\mathcal{O}$ of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), the localisation of the $\mathcal{O}$-base change of the Hecke lattice at the prime complement attached to $\theta$, is at most the rank of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131).
--
--   This is the inequality of ranks underlying the comparison of the Hecke algebra of level structure $S$ with the one of level structure $S_0$ at the maximal ideal cut out by $\bar\rho$ (the injectivity half of the identification of the anemic and full local Hecke algebras in Darmon–Diamond–Taylor §4.2, after Wiles). It is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq), where combined with surjectivity it gives an isomorphism of the two local Hecke algebras.
